    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The crash confirms the exact bug path:\n\n1. `decode_variable_length` at `mqtt.c:69` reads 1 byte past the buffer\n2. Called from `mg_mqtt_parse` at `mqtt.c:400`\n3. Triggered via the fuzz harness at `fuzz.c:38`\n\nThe 7-byte input `\\x30\\x05\\x00\\x00\\x80\\x80\\x80` is a crafted MQTT v5 PUBLISH packet where the properties variable-length encoding uses 3 continuation bytes (all with bit 0x80 set), causing `decode_variable_length` to attempt reading a 4th byte that's past the end of the buffer. The guard on line 398 (`p + 2 < end`) only ensures 3 bytes remain, which is insufficient.",
